A call chain continued with the member-access `:` leading the next line
is one statement: no `;` after the receiver line, the member names keep
their case (`:Replace` is not the keyword `:REPLACE`), and each chain line
takes one continuation level (fmt.indent_style and
fmt.semicolon_enforcement, issue #240 follow-up). Nested inside an :IF to
show the extra level is relative to the statement line.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE FillTemplate;
:PARAMETERS oTemplate, sTitle, sUser;
:DECLARE sOut;
:IF .NOT. Empty(sTitle);
sOut := oTemplate:ToString()
:Replace("##TITLE##", sTitle)
        :Replace("##USER##", sUser)
:Trim();
:ENDIF;
:RETURN sOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE FillTemplate;
	:PARAMETERS oTemplate, sTitle, sUser;
	:DECLARE sOut;
	:IF .NOT. Empty(sTitle);
		sOut := oTemplate:ToString()
			:Replace("##TITLE##", sTitle)
			:Replace("##USER##", sUser)
			:Trim();
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN sOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
